def knapsack(weights, values, capacity):
    dp = [0] * (capacity + 1)
    for w, v in zip(weights, values):
        for c in range(capacity, w - 1, -1):
            dp[c] = max(dp[c], dp[c - w] + v)
    return dp[capacity]
```
Iterating `c` from high to low ensures each item is only considered once (because `dp[c - w]` still reflects the previous row). Space drops from O(nC) to O(C).

